**Problem (diagnosed 2026-09-10):** slide quality regressed badly after the 4-phase planner refactor (commit `3e3c71b`) + "wire layout_pattern to layout selection" (`34338ab`). Root cause chain:
1. Fan-out per-slide planning (`fan_out_slide_plans`) removed cross-slide layout awareness — the old monolithic planner had an explicit adjacency rule; the per-slide prompt structurally cannot.
2. `enforce_layout_variety` (slide_component_planner.py) swaps `layout_pattern` on adjacent repeats but never updates `layout_hint` or checks `components`.
3. `_select_layout` now *obeys* that swapped pattern and injects a prescriptive `verified_example` POM snippet → generator gets a layout skeleton contradicting both the freeform `layout_hint` and the component list → overlap + dead whitespace. (Before `34338ab` the swap was a harmless no-op.)

`deck_nodes.py` is NOT a cause — it only concatenates + normalizes already-generated slide XML.

**User decisions (2026-09-10):** keep gpt-4.1 (no model upgrade); target ONE house style first = dense editorial business decks (4 example slides supplied, all compile+render well on v10.3.0 — see [[pom-offline-render-loop]]); full rework allowed; quality loop stays compile-only (no visual-critic repair for now). Theme system stays fixed-token-vocabulary for now (per-deck custom tokens deferred).

**Approach:** TEACH the house-style layout idiom + show a diverse gallery; REMOVE the machinery that constrains wrongly. NO archetypes / NO rigid scaffold — that contradicts the locked "component-based planning, full creative freedom" decision in [[project-production-plan]] and the user's explicit want ("dynamic llm free to generate any kind of slide; fixing layouts strips this"). The regression came from *adding* constraints (`34338ab`), not from too few.
- Phase 1: lock the 4 examples as compile-verified golden refs in `src/knowledge/examples/`; write `src/knowledge/core/house-style.yaml` — the composition GRAMMAR distilled from them (bands at `w="max"`; asymmetric `%` splits = content priority; repeated `w="max"` = equal; rigid nodes Chart/Matrix/ProcessArrow get `w="max"` + a fixed `h`; height-budget formula `720 − 2·pad − (bands−1)·gap` split by weight) + card recipes (surface-card / dark hero-panel / tinted callout w/ borderLeft|borderTop accent) + type ramp + spacing scale. Catalogue render-observed component limits into component YAMLs.
- Phase 2: `context_builder` — DELETE `_PATTERN_TO_LAYOUT` + the 12 `layouts/*.yaml` + single-`verified_example` injection. Replace with: always inject house-style.yaml grammar + a rotating gallery of 2-3 full diverse examples labelled "copy the vocabulary + the height math, never the structure".
- Phase 3: rewrite `generator/system.j2` around the grammar + gallery. Drop the "layout_hint = PRIMARY spatial instruction, follow exactly" pixel-arithmetic framing.
- Phase 4: `slide_component_planner` — `layout_hint` stays freeform but prompt asks for structure/priority language, not pixel widths/height-budgets. DELETE `enforce_layout_variety` (the enum-swap) and the sorter call in graph.py. Variety = a one-line prompt rule + optional warn-only post-check.
- Phase 5: `scripts/render_check.py` (built 2026-09-10) is the before/after harness + my dev-time iteration loop.

